[69.986, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead: phase-0-recon.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[69.996, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Phase 0: Recon \u2014 Detailed Procedures\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192Read this file at the start of Phase 0. It contains the complete step-by-step procedures, including mutation scanning, graph operations, pattern library scanning, architecture drift detection, and predictive recon.\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192## Recon Steps\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192Create `docs/holtz/` and `docs/holtz/recon/` if they do not exist. Each step is independent. Complete one, write its file, then start the next.\r\n         8\u2192\r\n         9\u2192| Step | Action | Output File |\r\n        10\u2192|------|--------|-------------|\r\n        11\u2192| 0a | Read project structure, docs, CLAUDE.md, architecture | `docs/holtz/recon/0a-project-overview.md` |\r\n        12\u2192| 0b | Identify test framework, runner, build system | `docs/holtz/recon/0b-test-infra.md` |\r\n        13\u2192| 0c | Run test suite, capture pass/fail/skip/time/coverage | `docs/holtz/recon/0c-test-baseline.md` |\r\n        14\u2192| 0d | Run linters/type checkers if configured | `docs/holtz/recon/0d-lint-results.md` |\r\n        15\u2192| 0e | Git churn analysis (top 20 most-changed files in last 50 commits) | `docs/holtz/recon/0e-churn.md` |\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (107 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.079, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead: impact-graph-operations.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.089, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Impact Graph Operations\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192Complete reference for all `impact_graph.py` CLI operations. The `--graph` flag is a **global argument** that must come BEFORE the subcommand.\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192## Graph Initialization (First Run)\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192The graph file is created automatically when you add the first node \u2014 `save()` creates parent directories and the file. Start adding nodes as you discover project entities during recon.\r\n         8\u2192\r\n         9\u2192```bash\r\n        10\u2192# First add_node creates docs/holtz/impact-graph.json\r\n        11\u2192python ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/holtz/scripts/impact_graph.py --graph docs/holtz/impact-graph.json add_node \"<module>:<function>\" \"function\" \"<file_path>\" --line <N>\r\n        12\u2192```\r\n        13\u2192\r\n        14\u2192## Graph Reconciliation (Subsequent Runs)\r\n        15\u2192\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (112 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.135, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead: status-file-format.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.145, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# docs/holtz/STATUS.md Format\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192This file is Holtz's program counter. Located at `docs/holtz/STATUS.md` in the target project. It is the first file read after any context compaction and the last file updated after completing any step.\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192## Template\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192```markdown\r\n         8\u2192# Holtz Status\r\n         9\u2192\r\n        10\u2192**Project:** {project name}\r\n        11\u2192**Started:** {ISO date}\r\n        12\u2192**Last Updated:** {ISO timestamp}\r\n        13\u2192**Iteration:** {N}\r\n        14\u2192\r\n        15\u2192## Current Position\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (65 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.194, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead: lens-registry.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[70.204, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Lens Registry\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192Analytical lenses for multi-perspective auditing. Holtz rotates through these during the convergence loop. True convergence requires all lenses clean in the same final sweep.\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192Users can add custom lenses by appending new sections following the same four-field format (Focus, Audit priorities, Failure modes, Entry point). Any `## heading` in this file with the four required fields is treated as a lens.\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192## component\r\n         8\u2192**Focus:** Individual functions, classes, modules in isolation\r\n         9\u2192**Audit priorities:** Correctness, edge cases, error handling, return values\r\n        10\u2192**Failure modes:** Logic errors, missing validation, unhandled edge cases\r\n        11\u2192**Entry point:** Standard Phases 1-3\r\n        12\u2192\r\n        13\u2192## integration\r\n        14\u2192**Focus:** Contracts and assumptions between modules\r\n        15\u2192**Audit priorities:** Interface agreements, shared state, data format assumptions, parser divergence\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (27 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
