[72.735, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Architecture Baseline\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192**Project:** holtz\r\n         4\u2192**Established:** 2026-03-22\r\n         5\u2192**Last Updated:** 2026-03-22\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192## Documented Intent\r\n         8\u2192\r\n         9\u2192README describes a two-layer architecture:\r\n        10\u21921. Markdown protocol layer (SKILL.md, references, patterns) consumed by the LLM\r\n        11\u21922. Python tool layer (CLI scripts) called by the LLM for concrete operations\r\n        12\u2192\r\n        13\u2192No CLAUDE.md or ARCHITECTURE.md exists. Intent is inferred from README, SKILL.md, and pyproject.toml.\r\n        14\u2192\r\n        15\u2192### Layering Rules\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (97 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.774, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mREADME.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.8, "o", "  \u001b[2mRead: README.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[72.811, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Holtz\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192A Claude Code plugin that audits your entire codebase, documents every defect in a structured punchlist, fixes them with TDD, and then does it again. And again. Until two consecutive passes find nothing new. You will think your code is clean. Holtz will disagree. He will keep disagreeing until he can't anymore, and then he will stop.\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192He will not apologize for any of it.\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192He works with a second auditor named Justine, who runs in parallel using a different methodology. She's breadth-first where he's depth-first. They don't coordinate during the audit. They merge after, and what each one missed becomes a map of the other's blind spots.\r\n         8\u2192\r\n         9\u2192## Why this exists\r\n        10\u2192\r\n        11\u2192Code review happens once. The comments get addressed, the reviewer approves, everyone moves on. But fixing a bug changes the terrain. A fix in module A shifts an assumption in module B, and now there's a new bug that didn't exist ten minutes ago. Nobody goes back to check. The PR is merged. CI is green. The bug ships.\r\n        12\u2192\r\n        13\u2192Holtz goes back to check.\r\n        14\u2192\r\n        15\u2192He runs a seven-phase audit and then starts over. Finds what the fixes uncovered. Fixes those too. Runs again. This continues until two consecutive passes produce zero new findings across nine analytical lenses. That's convergence. Everything before that is just progress.\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (198 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
