[82.915, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192# Recommendation Escalation Protocol\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192Before writing the recon summary, read the Recommendations section of every `docs/holtz/archive/*/SUMMARY.md` file (or `docs/holtz/archive/justine-*/SUMMARY.md` for Justine). Identify any recommendation that appears *in substance* (semantic match, not verbatim \u2014 e.g., \"add mypy\" and \"configure a type checker\" are the same recommendation) in 2 or more prior summaries. For each match, create a punchlist item. If the punchlist file does not exist yet, create it with proper file structure first (see punchlist-format.md File Structure section).\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192## Escalated Item Template\r\n         6\u2192\r\n         7\u2192````markdown\r\n         8\u2192### {ID}: {recommendation title}\r\n         9\u2192**Severity:** MEDIUM\r\n        10\u2192**Category:** design/inconsistency\r\n        11\u2192**Location:** docs/holtz/archive/*/SUMMARY.md\r\n        12\u2192**Status:** OPEN\r\n        13\u2192\r\n        14\u2192**Problem:** This recommendation has appeared in {N} consecutive audit summaries\r\n        15\u2192without being implemented: \"{recommendation text}\".\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (23 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
