[148.415, "o", "\u001b[2m    37\u2192**Target:** `pattern_brief_compact.py` \u2014 `parse_brief()` applies regex directly to content without masking\r\n        38\u2192**Predicted Issue:** code-fence-unaware-parsing \u2014 if a pattern brief contains a code example with a `## PAT-NNN:` header inside a code fence, `parse_brief` would match it as a real entry\r\n        39\u2192**Confidence:** MEDIUM\r\n        40\u2192**Basis:** parse_brief uses `header_re.finditer(content)` without masking. Pattern brief format includes `**Example:**` sections that could contain fenced code with pattern headers.\r\n        41\u2192**Lens:** component\r\n        42\u2192**Graph Support:** No `assumes` edges, no callers in graph\r\n        43\u2192**Outcome:**\r\n        44\u2192\r\n        45\u2192### Prediction 4\r\n        46\u2192**Target:** `README.md` \"What's inside\" line\u001b[0m\r\n"]
