[154.143, "o", "\u001b[2m    1\u2192\"\"\"Structural tests for compact pattern brief formats (CI-safe, no LLM calls).\"\"\"\r\n         2\u2192\r\n         3\u2192import pattern_brief_compact as pbc\r\n         4\u2192\r\n         5\u2192SAMPLE_BRIEF = \"\"\"\\\r\n         6\u2192# Holtz Pattern Brief\r\n         7\u2192\r\n         8\u2192> Read this before starting any audit work. These patterns were discovered\r\n         9\u2192> in prior audits of this project. Check for them in the code you're reviewing.\r\n        10\u2192\r\n        11\u2192## PAT-001: missing-edge-case-handling (Run 3, 2026-03-10)\r\n        12\u2192**What to look for:** Functions with early return on happy path that lack guards for null, empty, or boundary inputs. The error path exists but is never reached.\r\n        13\u2192**Detection heuristic:** `grep -rn 'if.*return' --include='*.py' | grep -v 'None\\\\|empty\\\\|boundary'`\r\n        14\u2192**Example:** A validation function returns True for valid input but has no branch for empty string \u2014 callers assume empty string is valid.\r\n        15\u2192\r\n    \u001b[2m    ... (69 more lines)\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\r\n"]
