[178.947, "o", "Both bugs confirmed. Prediction 1 (HIGH, `\\s*` regex) and Prediction 3 (MEDIUM, code-fence-unaware parsing) are real.\r\n\r\nNow let me audit the remaining source modules for Phase 3. I'll dispatch a subagent for the other source files while I write the findings for pattern_brief_compact.\r\n"]
[178.967, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m\u254c\u254c\u254c context: 144,218 tokens (cache read: 143,143, write: 1,074, output: 1) \u254c\u254c\u254c\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[179.974, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Agent\u001b[0m \u001b[2mAudit remaining source modules\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[203.796, "o", "  \u001b[2mAgent: Audit remaining source modules\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[203.806, "o", "\u001b[2m    **Status: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS**\r\n    \r\n    Wrote the audit report to `/Users/jonr/Documents/non-nitro-repos/holtz/docs/holtz/audit/3-adversarial-batch1.md`.\r\n    \r\n    **Summary of 21 findings across 9 files:**\r\n    \r\n    Three findings warrant fixes:\r\n    \r\n    1. **AV-1** (`hooks/artifact_verification.py` line 29) -- The `--graph` argument extraction regex misses `--graph=path` equals-sign syntax, which argparse accepts. The hook falls back to the default path and may emit a spurious warning about the wrong file. Fix: change `[ \\t]+` to `[= \\t]+` in the regex.\r\n    \r\n    2. **VP-1** (`validate_punchlist.py` lines 232-234) -- Acceptance criteria checkbox detection runs on masked content, while Problem/Evidence extraction uses `_section_from_original()` to get original content. This inconsistency means checkboxes inside code fences are invisible to the check. Should use `_section_from_original('Acceptance Criteria')` and check for checkboxes in the returned original content.\r\n    \r\n    3. **CC-1** (`convergence_check.py` lines 318-325) -- The partial deletion detector blocks convergence when items are legitimately consolidated (merged duplicates). The existing comment acknowledges \"equal-count replacement\" but not consolidation, which is a documented workflow.\r\n    \r\n    The remaining 18 findings are INFO/LOW severity -- correct behavior, documented tradeoffs, or negligible-risk edge cases. No convention violations found (`\\s` not used; all horizontal-whitespace regexes correctly use `[ \\t]`). No race conditions beyond the TOCTOU in `status_staleness_gate.py` which is already handled with try/except.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[204.369, "o", "Let me verify the three concerns from the subagent.\r\n"]
